+{"connection_id":"BC-00221d1d00f5720618c2","ref":"SBLGNT:2Cor.9.11","status":"rejected","reason":"Enrichment for generosity is stated, but this verse has no expressed juice or afflicted giver; 2 Corinthians 1:4-6 supplies the distress-to-gift sequence.","paragraphs":[10],"evidence":["SBLGNT:2Cor.9.11"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-f135db4054d1346ae2e8","ref":"SBLGNT:2Tim.2.21","status":"rejected","reason":"The vessel represents a cleansed person ready for work, not a container holding an extract; 2 Corinthians 4:7 is the more exact contained-value image.","paragraphs":[10],"evidence":["SBLGNT:2Tim.2.21"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-110340ab35d39c23880f","ref":"SBLGNT:2Tim.2.24","status":"rejected","reason":"Patience and teaching describe one servant's conduct; the verse lacks reciprocal counsel and the pressure-to-patience sequence.","paragraphs":[11],"evidence":["SBLGNT:2Tim.2.24"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-eed143316244e204fed3","ref":"SBLGNT:2Tim.2.25","status":"rejected","reason":"Gentle correction toward truth is one-directional instruction to an opponent; it does not pair mutual advice with patience as 1 Thessalonians 5:14 does.","paragraphs":[11],"evidence":["SBLGNT:2Tim.2.25"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-aaec69d05b8b7194bd6a","ref":"SBLGNT:2Tim.4.2","status":"rejected","reason":"The instruction to Timothy joins exhortation and patience, but addresses a single preacher; 1 Thessalonians 5:14 gives the selected communal form.","paragraphs":[11],"evidence":["SBLGNT:2Tim.4.2"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-c6a9994642000154e040","ref":"SBLGNT:2Tim.4.2","status":"rejected","reason":"This repeats the preacher's patient-exhortation proposal; the passage does not describe believers advising one another.","paragraphs":[11],"evidence":["SBLGNT:2Tim.4.2"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-d35187e455a094f51f5b","ref":"SBLGNT:2Tim.4.6","status":"rejected","reason":"Paul's being poured out is a cultic libation of his life, not sap squeezed under pressure; the paragraph's liquid is received rather than the person's sacrificial death.","paragraphs":[10],"evidence":["SBLGNT:2Tim.4.6"],"annotations":[]}
