+{"connection_id":"BC-4c259e02520a155ff076","ref":"SBLGNT:Rev.22.17","status":"rejected","reason":"Free water of life relieves thirst, but is neither pressed from fruit nor a bitter remedy made under pressure.","paragraphs":[10],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Rev.22.17"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-3cae991faff7a7ac8d24","ref":"SBLGNT:Rev.8.11","status":"rejected","reason":"Wormwood's lethal bitter water is a different apocalyptic event, not a counter-narrative of the Qur'anic prayer for patience.","paragraphs":[11],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Rev.8.11"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-c0d2ba965c65413a7bfe","ref":"SBLGNT:Rev.8.11","status":"rejected","reason":"The bitter water kills rather than heals; Exodus 15:23-26 provides the closer tree, bitter water, and healing sequence selected for this paragraph.","paragraphs":[11],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Rev.8.11"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-444fac8749039467ca94","ref":"SBLGNT:Rom.12.20","status":"rejected","reason":"Feeding and giving drink to an enemy repeats Proverbs 25:21; neither verse describes the pressed essence or distress producing transferable consolation.","paragraphs":[10],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Rom.12.20"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-117af5d49a2c55119039","ref":"SBLGNT:Rom.12.21","status":"rejected","reason":"Overcoming evil with good is a moral summary after the drink instruction, but adds no concrete pressure, extraction, or stored liquid.","paragraphs":[10],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Rom.12.21"],"annotations":[]}
