+{"connection_id":"BC-84c47f52fb6f4e1140db","ref":"WLC:Ps.34.11","status":"rejected","reason":"The second proposal repeats want versus provision; Psalm 8 places the relevant human and lack roots in the same two-verse unit.","paragraphs":[11],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.34.11"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-b94fdd7335a911523298","ref":"WLC:Ps.39.7","status":"rejected","reason":"צבר means heaping wealth without knowing who will collect it; Joseph's grain in Genesis 41:49 gives a closer storage scene and the same semantic limit against Arabic sabr.","paragraphs":[12],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.39.7"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-1f624107c80ea1aecdac","ref":"WLC:Ps.69.22","status":"rejected","reason":"Enemies give poison for food and vinegar for thirst; these aggravate suffering and do not make an acrid medicine from a pressed tree.","paragraphs":[11],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.69.22"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-2b36dc8010f83ad0465a","ref":"WLC:Ps.75.9","status":"rejected","reason":"The cup of foaming wine and dregs is divine judgment on the wicked, not a medicinal essence held for use after pressure; Revelation 14 gives the sharper press itself.","paragraphs":[12],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.75.9"],"annotations":[]}
